Third-party attributions
------------------------

Several implementation units are ports, adaptations, or drop-in replacements
for algorithms from other permissively licensed projects. The local source
headers identify the affected units.

BearSSL

  Portions of the RSA and P-256 code are ported from BearSSL implementations
  by Thomas Pornin. BearSSL is distributed under the MIT License.

Fiat-Crypto

  The Fiat P-256 and Curve25519 field arithmetic units are generated or ported
  from Fiat-Crypto style formally verified arithmetic. The source headers
  identify these as MIT/PLV-derived arithmetic.

SPARKNaCl

  Several APIs, software fallbacks, and compatibility paths depend on or adapt
  SPARKNaCl algorithms and types. SPARKNaCl is published in Alire as
  BSD-3-Clause and should be credited according to its upstream license files.
